    {
      "id": "18600",
      "key": "SFCC-307",
      "summary": "Inventory",
      "description": "Epic Name:\n Inventory\\n\\n\nEpic Summary\n\\n\\nThis epic covers the inventory data integration and availability logic underpinning the Zimmermann PWA Kit storefront. It includes the full and delta inventory feed from NewStore OMS via MuleSoft, aggregated available-to-promise (ATP) stock calculation, buffer stock threshold configuration, and the availability states surfaced across PDP, PLP, and cart. It provides the inventory infrastructure that all other epics depend on for accurate stock display.\\n\\n\nBusiness Value / Objective\n\\n\\nAccurate, real-time inventory availability is critical to Zimmermann's customer experience and operational integrity. Getting the inventory feed, ATP aggregation, and buffer stock logic right at go-live ensures customers see correct availability states across all 8 storefronts, reduces overselling risk, and gives the merchandising team direct control over stock display thresholds without requiring a code deployment.\\n\\n\nScope\n\\n\\nIn Scope:\\n\\n- Full daily inventory feed from NewStore OMS via MuleSoft into SFCC\\n- Configurable delta inventory feed (confirmed: 15-minute intervals)\\n- Aggregated ATP stock calculation per SKU per region across all eligible warehouses and boutiques\\n- Buffer stock threshold logic applied at SFCC level to derive availability state from ATP figure\\n- Business Manager configuration of buffer stock threshold per SKU per storefront\\n- Bulk upload support for buffer stock threshold configuration\\n- PDP availability states driven by buffer threshold (Add to Bag, Out of Stock)\\n- Low stock indicator at size level on PDP below configurable threshold\\n- Back-in-stock email notification submission to Emarsys\\n- Out-of-stock product suppression configuration on PLP\\n- Real-time boutique stock availability for Find in Boutique (OMS call via MuleSoft)\\n- Find in Boutique OMS response caching with configurable TTL\\n\\nOut of Scope:\\n\\n- Cart page OOS notification and inventory check at checkout — covered in SFCC-11 (Cart & Inventory)\\n- Find in Boutique and Collect in Boutique frontend component build — covered in SFCC-5 (PDP) and SFCC-12 (Checkout)\\n- NewStore OMS configuration and warehouse routing logic — Zimmermann/NewStore responsibility\\n- MuleSoft feed development — MuleSoft team responsibility\\n- Einstein recommendations — covered in SFCC-7 (Search & Recommendations)\\n\\n\nDependencies\n\\n\\n- MuleSoft team — inventory feed endpoints and real-time OMS call endpoints must be defined and available in a test environment before stories can be built and tested\\n- NewStore OMS — source of truth for all inventory data\\n- SFCC-5 (PDP) — PDP availability state stories depend on buffer threshold logic being in place\\n- SFCC-6 (PLP) — OOS suppression story depends on buffer threshold logic being in place\\n- Emarsys — back-in-stock notification endpoint and payload structure must be confirmed\\n- Tim Lavelle / Integration lead — confirm whether ATP aggregation is performed by MuleSoft before delivery to SFCC or by SFCC post-receipt\\n\\n\nAssumptions & Constraints\n\\n\\n- NewStore OMS is the source of truth for all inventory data; all inventory calls are routed through MuleSoft — no direct SFCC-to-OMS connection\\n- Buffer stock threshold is applied at SFCC level; raw inventory feed values from MuleSoft are unchanged\\n- ATP aggregation ownership (MuleSoft vs SFCC) is an open item pending confirmation from the integration lead\\n- Find in Boutique displays true physical boutique stock — buffer threshold does not apply\\n- Inventory feed setup (SFCC-288) and ATP aggregation (SFCC-289) may not warrant full user stories — pending confirmation from Tim Lavelle on whether these are covered in the integration runbook or technical design document",
      "status": {
