      "id": "18142",
      "key": "SFCC-97",
      "summary": "Navigation Menu — Mobile Hamburger & Drill-Down",
      "description": "As a\n Shopper,\nI want\n to open a navigation menu from a hamburger icon on mobile and drill down through headings to reach subcategories,\nso that\n I can find and navigate to the right section of the site without needing a full desktop layout.\nReference Image (Figma is leading):\n\n\nContext:\nOn mobile, the global header collapses the navigation into a hamburger menu icon. Tapping it opens a full navigation panel. Rather than showing all levels at once, the navigation uses a drill-down pattern — the shopper taps a top-level heading to reveal its subcategories, and can continue navigating deeper into the hierarchy. A back control allows them to return to the previous level.\nKey behaviours:\nTapping the hamburger icon opens the mobile navigation panel\nThe panel displays top-level navigation categories\nTapping a category that has subcategories drills into that category, replacing the top-level view with the subcategory list\nA back control is visible at the top of the panel to return to the previous level\nZ.Immerse functions as a direct link and does not drill down\nThe 'Back in Boutique' category is included in the nav\nTapping a destination link closes the panel and navigates to the relevant page\nNav items are CMS-managed; adding or removing items does not require a code change\nThis story is design-dependent — the panel layout, animation, and drill-down transition behaviour must come from the Figma spec before implementation begins.",
