    {
      "id": "17835",
      "key": "SFCC-9",
      "summary": "Store Locator",
      "description": "Epic Summary\n\n\nThis epic builds the store locator and boutique detail experience on the SFCC platform, allowing shoppers to find Zimmermann boutiques by location across all regional storefronts. It covers the store locator page with map and list views, boutique search, store detail pages with live opening hours, directions, and real-time Find in Boutique stock availability.\nBusiness Value / Objective\n\n\nZimmermann operates over 70 boutiques globally and the store locator is a key touchpoint connecting the digital and physical brand experience. Providing shoppers with accurate, real-time boutique information — including opening hours, directions, and in-store product availability — supports omnichannel engagement and drives foot traffic to boutiques.\nScope\nIn Scope\nStore locator page: map and list view of boutiques, boutique search by location, distance-based results\nStore detail page: boutique name, address, phone, opening hours, live open/closed status, directions link via Google Maps\nOpening hours sourced from daily Google Business API feed, with a manual override option in Business Manager for public holidays or temporary closures\nGoogle Maps integration for map display and directions on the store locator and store detail pages\nLocalBusiness structured data schema on boutique detail pages for SEO (per Sparro schema template)\nFind in Boutique: real-time stock availability per boutique for a product in context on the store detail page, sourced from NewStore via MuleSoft\nBoutique data attributes stored and managed in SFCC Store Inventory module: name, address, phone, coordinates, storefront, store type, BOPIS flag, opening hours, opening hours override\nOut of Scope\nCollect in Boutique (BOPIS) checkout flow — covered in SFCC-12 Checkout Flow & Delivery\nFind in Boutique slide-out on PDP — covered in SFCC-5 Product Detail Page (PDP)\nGoogle Business profile management and maintenance — Zimmermann responsibility\nGTM/analytics events for store locator interactions — covered in SFCC-22 SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing\nInside Chat on store detail pages — covered in SFCC-88 Client Services\nDependencies\nSFCC-4 Product Catalogue — boutique stock data requires product variants to be available in SFCC before Find in Boutique can be tested end-to-end\nSFCC-12 Checkout Flow & Delivery — BOPIS flag on boutiques must align with checkout collect in boutique configuration\nMuleSoft / NewStore — real-time Find in Boutique stock availability is sourced from NewStore via MuleSoft; integration must be available for end-to-end testing\nGoogle Business API — approach for opening hours feed (API vs manual export) must be confirmed before build; who maintains Google Business profiles (eComm vs retail ops) also TBC\nZimmermann — complete and accurate boutique list with all required store attributes must be provided before store data can be loaded into SFCC\nAssumptions & Constraints\nBoutiques are available on AU, UK, and EU domestic storefronts only at launch; other storefronts TBC\nGoogle Business API integration approach is under review — a manual feed file import may be used as an alternative if API access is not confirmed in time\nStore type values (Boutique, Outlet, Concession) to be confirmed with Zimmermann before store data load\nOpening hours override is an exception-based field managed in Business Manager for holiday trading or temporary closures\nFind in Boutique is available on NewStore-live stores only at launch; availability will expand as NewStore rolls out to additional markets\nPriority:\n Medium\nTarget Release / Sprint:\n Sprint 5",
      "status": {
        "name": "To Do",
        "category": "To Do",
        "color": "blue-gray"
      },
      "issue_type": {
        "name": "Epic"
